<title>USA: Canon U.S. unit cuts Innova PC line prices.</title>
<headline>Canon U.S. unit cuts Innova PC line prices.</headline>
<dateline>COSTA MESA, Calif. 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canon Computer Systems Inc, a unit of Canon Inc, said Monday it has lowered prices on its Innova desktop system and multimedia notebook computers by as much as 18 percent.</p>
<p>The company said the products carry new estimated street prices ranging from $1,399 to $2,899.</p>
<p>The computers feature 12x speed compact disc players, and are based on Intel Corp Pentium chips running at speeds of up to 200 megahertz and up to 3.1 gigabyte hard drives.</p>
<p>-- E. Auchard New York newsdesk, 212-859-1736</p>
